{"skill":{"slug":"agent-phone-call","displayName":"Agent Phone Call"},"version":{"version":"1.0.5","createdAt":1776332821052,"changelog":"No changes detected in this version.\n\n- No file or documentation changes were made.\n- Version remains at 1.0.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":22162,"sha256":"8db52e6c9ef016e799b2ee7291614e6cadadd52a95b1867bb0d3c12d59f1f27c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/activation.sh","size":1568,"sha256":"5d41e2e7c763dec6c3901f982f91c721ab4055a39dd77fd3702ca32bdf658e01","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/inbound.sh","size":1823,"sha256":"99f537738bc6eef4140ad50d76b1d542c7bf8450fb4a76b9b1cc29501e70e31a","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/balance.sh","size":1448,"sha256":"fe38bbf6ef75c26e0131c491074167e08edf38991357992bd0dc3ced5d8ee277","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/query.sh","size":1108,"sha256":"4cf8e91e4b0905c24dccd71ffc9ca7d2493573b70d1ac73aec3bb940cdd5952f","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/prompt_update.sh","size":1529,"sha256":"c64868fd7ab7c1b7681b2b0d78a7a852bdc4291a5153f063426c6a60b4228167","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/send.sh","size":1824,"sha256":"d276444729af03bbe13cc76d9a9ae58fb1bcab01b1b1fd0b06fd56a8d5cef1df","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2544,"sha256":"50cfed1a89906af8e82b3a7b1b6a7c2e827734de116142225e0bc5267385b531","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789533732555,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a7201c524702cfa0c551bf99b4ac782f137067024b03ad5bccaf26ba1b543634","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a7201c524702cfa0c551bf99b4ac782f137067024b03ad5bccaf26ba1b543634","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090446603},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":28,"checkedAt":1789533732555},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent phone-calling integration, but it under-discloses sensitive call recording/transcript handling and pushes broad activation, full transcript sharing, scheduled polling, and promotional sharing behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Declared access is narrow in filesystem scope and domain scope, but the data handled is high sensitivity: phone numbers, caller identities, call content, recordings, summaries, and account balance data are sent to or retrieved from a third-party service.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains local shell scripts and declares PollyReach network endpoints and the local token file; no remote code execution or hidden installer was found. Registration creates a PollyReach trust relationship and stores a bearer token in ~/.config/PollyReach/key.json.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Triggers include broad phrases such as make a call and help me book; the runtime instructions mandate full target/caller information and line-by-line transcripts, require branded/top-up/referral messaging, and include a sharing message pointing other agents to a mutable remote SKILL.md.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No root-level runtime behavior or persistent service is shipped; sudo appears only as dependency-install guidance for jq. The skill does persist a bearer token and recommends user-approved scheduled polling for inbound calls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The network API calls, token storage, calling, inbound answering, recordings, transcripts, and balance checks fit the stated phone-call purpose, but the artifact encourages collecting phone numbers, public number sharing, and automatic inbound answering without an up-front privacy and consent notice for users or callers.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this carefully before installing. It can place and answer calls through PollyReach, store an auth token locally, and expose phone numbers, transcripts, recordings, summaries, and caller details to a third-party service and to the agent chat. Do not use it for calls involving sensitive personal, financial, medical, legal, or confidential business information unless you understand consent, recording, retention, and caller-notice obligations. Avoid publicizing the assigned number or enabling scheduled polling without explicit control over what gets recorded and reported.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Confirmed in SKILL.md: the skill asks users to share phone numbers and publicize the assigned number while inbound calls may generate summaries, transcripts, recordings, and caller details; privacy disclosure and consent controls are not prominent enough for that workflow.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: Confirmed in SKILL.md: outbound and inbound reports are required to include full phone/caller details and line-by-line transcripts by default, which is broader than necessary for most call-status reporting.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The activation guidance is broader than ideal for a sensitive telephony tool because common phrases can trigger registration or call workflows, although the skill does say not to use it for casual mentions.\n[E1] expected: External transmission to api.pollyreach.ai and use of a stored bearer token are core to the disclosed phone-call service, but remain important sensitive-data risks for users to understand.\n[P3] expected: The cited polling instruction is part of retrieving call results after a user-directed send operation; it does not show covert exfiltration, but it reinforces that user task content goes to PollyReach.\n[SDI-2] expected: The standalone script reads the PollyReach token and contacts the PollyReach API, which is justified by the surrounding SKILL.md manifest and script purpose declarations.\n[PE2] expected: The sudo matches are dependency installation hints for jq, not runtime privilege escalation by the skill scripts.\n[T01] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: required branded language, top-up/referral prompts, and remote SKILL.md sharing are not necessary for neutral call result reporting, though no safety bypass or local compromise was found.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789533732555}}}}}